0..78 Comment "//! A group\'s laws stated as rules, the coincidence check certifying each with"
79..158 Comment "//! the others: the structure the circle\'s loops carry under composition, whose"
159..234 Comment "//! laws `circle-group.gandr` proves as paths. The written laws do not join"
235..304 Comment "//! among themselves: the cancellation `mul(inv(x), x) ==> e()` meets"
305..385 Comment "//! associativity at `mul(mul(inv(x), x), z)`, which the two leave at `z` and at"
386..466 Comment "//! `mul(inv(x), mul(x, z))`. Completion orients each such pair into a rule that"
467..542 Comment "//! follows from the written ones, certified by the pair\'s two paths, until"
543..623 Comment "//! every pair joins [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras], § 7."
624..697 Comment "//! The row reads a law no written rule states, the inverse of a product."
698..701 Comment "//!"
702..717 Comment "//! - see: #338"
718..783 Comment "//! - cites: [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]"
784..787 Comment "//!"
788..959 Comment "//! [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]: https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-012975-4.50028-X \"Knuth and Bendix, Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras\""
961..1038 Comment "/// A group\'s unit, associativity and inverse laws, each a rule: `e()` is the"
1039..1117 Comment "/// unit and `a()`, `b()` two elements the row reads; the row\'s normal form is"
1118..1154 Comment "/// one only a derived rule reaches."
1155..1157 Other "@["
1158..1168 Other "normalizes"
1168..1169 Other "("
1169..1170 StringLit "\""
1170..1207 StringLit "inv(mul(a, b)) ~> mul(inv(b), inv(a))"
1207..1208 StringLit "\""
